/save no longer silently overwrites a file it didn't write. It's committed as c1d927ff, titled "Part of #1211" rather than "Fixes", because task 2 owns /spawn -o.

The bug: I ran the built binary before changing anything, in a temporary directory with a.md containing hi. /save a.md printed "session saved" and a.md then held []. I posted that result to #1211 before editing any code.

What changed:
• /save replaces a file without asking only if this yoyo process saved it with /save or loaded it with /load or --continue. Paths are compared after resolving them. Saving again as you work needs no flag.
• Any other existing file is left alone, and yoyo prints: <path> already exists. Nothing was written. To replace it: /save <path> --force (or choose another file name).
• A directory is always refused, and that message doesn't offer --force.
• Without --force, the file is created only if nothing is at that path yet, as /export does. A file that appears in the meantime, or a broken symlink, is not written through.
• The argument parsing and refusal messages are now shared with /export.

Checks:
• Built binary after the change: a foreign a.md is refused and still holds hi. --force replaces it. Saving new.json twice in one session works. A new session is refused on new.json until it runs /load new.json, then /save new.json works. An earlier run where commands seemed to vanish was a test setup problem: input piped in all at once got dropped. With paced input, all four cases behave as above.
• New tests: 13 in src/commands_session_save_tests.rs. One feeds the printed --force command back through the parser and checks it names the same file.
• Broken-on-purpose runs: breaking only the refuse/allow decision turned just the decision-table test red. The file-writing tests stayed green because the "create only if new" step caught the overwrite on its own. Breaking both layers, which is the old behaviour, turned 4 tests red. With the code restored, all 13 pass and no marker is left.
• Full gate: cargo fmt, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings and cargo test all pass. The first test run failed a lock-handling check in tests/lock_recovery_chokepoint.rs; the new code now uses sync_util::lock_or_recover as that check requires. commands_session.rs is 1985 lines, under its 2000 cap.

Docs: updated the /save help text, the short help line, docs/src/features/sessions.md, docs/src/usage/commands.md and the README commands table. There is no yoyo save shell command.

Still open on #1211: --save-session <path> in src/main.rs also overwrites a file you name without checking. The ticket's census only searched src/commands_*.rs, so it missed this one. Fixing it needs its own decision, because scripts may reuse the same --save-session path on purpose. I left it unchanged and commented on #1211 so task 2's Fixes for /spawn -o doesn't close the ticket with this still open.
